{"title":"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The expression <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/4/5b46aae763de06f8fe0cb297f2ab1851ec4c6752.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{3} + 2^{2} + 2^{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"96\" height=\"18\" /> is equal to\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/a/ddad92641b78208b579bd74d80dedc44fd007748.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 6 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 10 \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 14 \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 18 \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 22$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"387\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Following <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Order_of_operations\" title=\"Order of operations\">order of operations</a>, we have:\n</p><p>\t\\begin{align*}\n\t\t2^{3} + 2^{2} + 2^{1} &amp;= 8 + 2^{2} + 2^{1}\\\\\n\t\t&amp;= 8 + 4 + 2^{1}\\\\\n\t\t&amp;= 8 + 4 + 2\\\\\n\t\t&amp;= 12 + 2\\\\\n\t\t&amp;=\\boxed {\\textbf {(C)}\\ 14}\n\t\\end{align*}\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can realize that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/3/5e34281581291a368fd56fe973a3ddc8def7fe7f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{1}$\" width=\"14\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/2/df290664cf90881dec7ee8d27f6da0910eb8f1fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"17\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/2/642dea81077b775f66619c0b093d5e3ac52c9df7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{3}$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> form a geometric sequence with first term <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/5/16514fc9f5a6ef10b94c7d0624dff1fdc7458daa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{1} = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" /> and common ratio <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/e/b4e1601cec996498721fc1934cd55923bfc4401c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = \\frac{2^{2}}{2^{1}} = \\frac{2^{3}}{2^{2}} = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"133\" height=\"41\" />. Thus, the sum is\n</p><p>\\begin{align*}\n\t\t\\dfrac{2\\times \\left( 2^{3}-1 \\right)}{2-1} &amp;= \\dfrac{2\\times (8-1)}{1}\\\\\n\t\t&amp;= 2 \\times 7\\\\\n\t\t&amp;= \\boxed {\\textbf {(C)}\\ 14}.\n\\end{align*}\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley\">2013 CEMC Cayley</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?ti